Best-effort reading of other wire formats (display only) for dspi-core.

Why: the core reads exactly V32. Against any other firmware the app showed
nothing: an older image is shorter than 6136 bytes, so the chunked read ran
past its end, the firmware STALLed it and fetch_all failed outright ("settings
could not be read", compat stayed UNKNOWN); a newer image was cut at 6136
bytes (leaving the device's snapshot session open) and rejected as TOO_NEW.
The firmware's layout history since the V16 break is small and regular
(sections appended; reserved bytes claimed; two in-place growths, V18 leveller
+4 and V28 input-config S/PDIF pin array +1), so older images can be mapped
onto the V32 layout exactly, and a newer image's V32 prefix can be shown.
Design and survey: ../docs/WIRE-FORMAT-COMPAT.md (dspi-mobile).

NOTHING here enables a write. compat stays TOO_OLD/TOO_NEW for these images
(every existing gate keeps refusing writes), bulk_valid stays false (so
apply_all_params refuses; it now also checks the version), and notifications
only trigger a re-read, never an offset patch.

Hunks:
1. core/src/wirecompat.rs (new): WIRE_READ_*, WIRE_FEAT_* + wire_features(v),
   bulk_size(v), image_length(header), normalize(image) (V16..V31 -> V32
   layout; newer -> V32 prefix after a plausibility check),
   decode_bulk_compat(); unit tests.
2. core/src/protocol.rs: decode_bulk keeps its strict V32 contract; its body
   moves to decode_image() so wirecompat can reuse it. Sets wire_read/features.
3. core/src/state.rs: DspState.wire_read, DspState.wire_features.
4. core/src/commands.rs: read_bulk_chunked reads the header's payload_length
   (unchanged for V32); fetch_all decodes any supported version and, for a
   display-only image, reads only the preset directory and names on top;
   apply_all_params refuses a non-V32 state.
5. core/src/notify.rs: display-only state: a PARAM_CHANGED or invalidation
   re-reads the image (no capture_baseline).
6. core/src/lib.rs: pub mod wirecompat.

Upstream form: identical, separable (one new module plus small hooks); the
C ABI gains the two DspState fields (repr(C), regenerate the Qt header).

